---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ChapterNav from '../components/ChapterNav.astro';
/* R227 [§S3]: the interior of every trajectory rests on one fitted scalar, and
   until now the page published the results without saying so. Every figure in
   the note below is read from the model, never typed. */
import {
  KAPPA_MATURE_PCT, KAPPA_SOURCE_FLOOR_PCT, KAPPA_SOURCE_GATE, KAPPA_VALUE
} from '../lib/equations';
import { kappaBand } from '../lib/kappa-check';
import { QUALITY_DATA } from '../lib/quality';

const kppTppCount = QUALITY_DATA.parameters.filter((p) => p.type !== 'CP').length;
const kappaMetricsMoved = Math.max(...kappaBand().map((r) => r.metricsMoved));
---
<BaseLayout title="National Health Assurance: Quality">
  <main>

  <section class="card">
    <h2>The complete controlled parameter catalog</h2>
    <p class="desc">The plan controls three different kinds of
      parameters. Key performance parameters define system outcomes,
      technical performance parameters define operating performance, and
      cost parameters define the quantities required to cost, calibrate, and
      stress-test the system. This view lists all 440 records in the
      controlled dictionaries and groups them by where they matter.</p>
    <div class="quality-counts" aria-label="Controlled parameter counts">
      <div class="quality-count">
        <span class="quality-kicker">System outcomes</span>
        <strong>45</strong>
        <b>KPP records</b>
        <small>Coverage, access, quality, equity, fiscal, transition, workforce, and legitimacy outcomes</small>
      </div>
      <div class="quality-count">
        <span class="quality-kicker">Operating performance</span>
        <strong>85</strong>
        <b>TPP records</b>
        <small>Eligibility, payment, medicines, facilities, workforce, benefits, data, cyber, rights, and innovation</small>
      </div>
      <div class="quality-count">
        <span class="quality-kicker">Cost and model control</span>
        <strong>310</strong>
        <b>CP records in 20 families</b>
        <small>Inputs, states, ledgers, derived outputs, offsets, units, owners, and calibration status</small>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="note"><b>How to read “target.”</b> KPP and TPP source targets
      are maturity targets unless the rollout plan assigns an earlier
      milestone or gate floor. CP records are model controls rather than
      performance targets; the catalog preserves their value/calibration
      status and never invents a phase value.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="card">
    <h2>Targets across the twelve-year rollout</h2>
    <p class="desc">Every KPP and TPP carries a target at every phase
      where it is measurable, built from three sources in priority order:
      the plan's own gate floors and milestones (authoritative, shown
      below), the Data tab's hand-derived information-mesh plan (reused
      verbatim so the two tabs always agree), and a calculated value from
      that parameter's own equation for everything else. The panel and
      table here show only the plan's explicit floors; each parameter's
      full phase-by-phase strip, including the equation-derived targets,
      lives in the explorer.</p>
    <div id="quality-phase-overview" class="quality-phase-overview"
      aria-label="Numeric parameter milestones and gate floors across rollout phases"></div>
    <div id="quality-floor-table" class="tbl-scroll quality-floor-wrap"></div>
    <p class="note"><b>How equation-derived targets are built.</b>
      Each parameter's equation combines the cost model's sourced inputs,
      the rollout build state at that phase (coverage, cost-sharing
      elimination, units, pharmacy, hospitals, expanded benefits, and
      infrastructure), and other performance parameters it depends on.
      The equation explorer below shows every formula and how results flow
      from one parameter into the next. Where an equation would cross one
      of the plan's committed floors or milestones, the committed value
      holds, so targets never regress between phases.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="card">
    <h2>The equation behind every target</h2>
    <p class="desc">Targets here are calculated, not asserted. Pick a
      stress scenario from the healthcare model and every equation
      recomputes: the same inputs that move total system cost also move
      what each phase can credibly demand. Pick a diagram to see how
      equations feed each other, reading left to right from model inputs
      through operating parameters (TPP) to system outcomes (KPP). Select
      any node for its formula, inputs, and phase-by-phase values.</p>
    <div class="quality-controls" role="group" aria-label="Equation explorer controls">
      <label class="quality-control">
        <span>Stress scenario</span>
        <select id="quality-eq-scenario"></select>
      </label>
      <label class="quality-control">
        <span>Diagram</span>
        <select id="quality-eq-group"></select>
      </label>
      <label class="quality-control">
        <span>Phase for input values</span>
        <select id="quality-eq-phase">
          <option value="P0">P0 (Year 1)</option>
          <option value="P1">P1 (Year 2)</option>
          <option value="P2">P2 (Year 3)</option>
          <option value="P3">P3 (Year 4)</option>
          <option value="P4">P4 (Year 6)</option>
          <option value="P5">P5 (Year 7)</option>
          <option value="P6">P6 (Year 8)</option>
          <option value="P7">P7 (Year 10)</option>
          <option value="P8" selected>P8 (Year 12)</option>
        </select>
      </label>
    </div>
    <p id="quality-eq-groupdesc" class="note quality-eq-groupdesc"></p>
    <p class="note">How far short of maturity a target sits at each interior
      phase is set by one number, the immaturity stress multiplier
      (kappa = {KAPPA_VALUE}). It is fitted to a single controlled
      observation: Gate {KAPPA_SOURCE_GATE} requires high-stakes AI review and
      audit capture of {KAPPA_SOURCE_FLOOR_PCT}% at P5 against
      {KAPPA_MATURE_PCT}% at maturity. Maturity targets do not depend on it;
      every interim target on {kappaMetricsMoved} of the {kppTppCount} metrics
      does. At half and double that multiplier the typical interim target
      moves a few percent and the widest moves a great deal more, which is
      published as a sensitivity band in the methodology. Nothing else in the
      plan tests the choice.</p>
    <div class="quality-eq-legend" aria-hidden="true">
      <span class="quality-eq-chip chip-param">cost model input</span>
      <span class="quality-eq-chip chip-ramp">rollout build state</span>
      <span class="quality-eq-chip chip-model">fiscal engine value</span>
      <span class="quality-eq-chip chip-index">derived index</span>
      <span class="quality-eq-chip chip-tpp">TPP</span>
      <span class="quality-eq-chip chip-kpp">KPP</span>
    </div>
    <div id="quality-eq-diagram" class="quality-eq-diagram tbl-scroll"
      aria-label="Traversable equation flow diagram"></div>
    <div id="quality-eq-detail" class="quality-eq-detail" aria-live="polite"></div>
    <p class="note"><b>Reading the diagrams.</b> KPPs sit at the far right
      unless they feed another equation. Values shown for inputs use the
      selected phase and scenario. Committed floors, milestones, and the
      Data tab's plan stay authoritative in the catalog below; under a
      stress scenario the explorer shows what the equations say the system
      could actually deliver, which is the honest gap a gate review would
      have to confront.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="card">
    <h2>Explore all 440 parameters</h2>
    <p class="desc">Search the controlled identifier or text, narrow the
      catalog by parameter type or concept, and choose a rollout phase. Select
      any row for its calculation, owner, datasets, status, its target
      equation, and the complete phase-by-phase target strip. With a stress
      scenario active in the explorer above, equation-derived targets in the
      strip and table recompute for that scenario.</p>
    <div class="quality-controls" role="group" aria-label="Quality catalog filters">
      <label class="quality-control quality-search">
        <span>Search</span>
        <input id="quality-search" type="search"
          placeholder="ID, metric, owner, dataset, family…">
      </label>
      <label class="quality-control">
        <span>Parameter type</span>
        <select id="quality-type">
          <option value="all">All types</option>
          <option value="KPP">KPP: key performance</option>
          <option value="TPP">TPP: technical performance</option>
          <option value="CP">CP: cost/model parameter</option>
        </select>
      </label>
      <label class="quality-control">
        <span>Concept or application</span>
        <select id="quality-concept">
          <option value="all">All concepts</option>
        </select>
      </label>
      <label class="quality-control">
        <span>Rollout phase shown</span>
        <select id="quality-phase">
          <option value="all">Source / maturity value</option>
          <option value="P0">P0 (Year 1)</option>
          <option value="P1">P1 (Year 2)</option>
          <option value="P2">P2 (Year 3)</option>
          <option value="P3">P3 (Year 4)</option>
          <option value="P4">P4 (Year 6)</option>
          <option value="P5">P5 (Year 7)</option>
          <option value="P6">P6 (Year 8)</option>
          <option value="P7">P7 (Year 10)</option>
          <option value="P8">P8 (Year 12)</option>
        </select>
      </label>
    </div>
    <div class="quality-filter-foot">
      <p id="quality-results" aria-live="polite"></p>
      <button id="quality-reset" class="btn" type="button">Reset filters</button>
    </div>

    <div id="quality-selected" class="quality-selected"
      aria-live="polite" aria-label="Selected parameter details"></div>

    <div class="tbl-scroll quality-table-wrap">
      <table class="data quality-table" id="quality-table">
        <caption class="sr-only">Complete controlled quality and cost parameter catalog</caption>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>

  <p class="rollout-source">The catalog covers the complete key-performance
    and technical-performance dictionaries, the 310-record cost-parameter
    registry, and the controlled phase and gate tables.
    <a href="https://github.com/mikehalvorson/US-National-Health-Assurance-System" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Sources and methodology</a>.</p>

    <ChapterNav />
  </main>
</BaseLayout>

<script>
  import '../scripts/quality-client.ts';
</script>
